  "text": "Welcome to The Pet Hospital (Parkway) | Veterinarians in Hattiesburg\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout\nOur Hospital\nWhy Trust Us?\nOur Vets\nOur Team\nLab\nCore Care\nVaccinations & Prevention\nWellness Exams\nDental Care\nInternal Medicine\nAcupuncture & Holistic Care\nCold Laser Therapy\nExotic Pets\nCancer Care\nPuppies & Kittens\nGeriatric Care\nSurgery\nSurgical Services\nSpaying & Neutering\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nOrthopedic Surgery\nC-Sections\nEmergencies\nPatients\nPatient Information\nFear Free Certified Vets\nFinancing Options\nPet Care Tips & Advice\nCareers\nShop\nContact\nSearch\nSearch\nFacebook\nGoogleBusiness\nSkip to Main Content\nAccessible Version\nStandard Version\nFacebook\nGoogleBusiness\n2010 Evelyn Gandy Pkwy\nHattiesburg\nMS\n39401\nUS\nBook Online\n(601) 544-3290\nAbout\nOur Hospital\nWhy Trust Us?\nOur Vets\nOur Team\nLab\nCore Care\nVaccinations & Prevention\nWellness Exams\nDental Care\nInternal Medicine\nAcupuncture & Holistic Care\nCold Laser Therapy\nExotic Pets\nCancer Care\nPuppies & Kittens\nGeriatric Care\nSurgery\nSurgical Services\nSpaying & Neutering\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nOrthopedic Surgery\nC-Sections\nEmergencies\nPatients\nPatient Information\nFear Free Certified Vets\nFinancing Options\nPet Care Tips & Advice\nCareers\nShop\nContact\nOpen Search Dialog\nLimited Time Offer\nEnjoy a $25 First Exam – Learn More\n×\nClose\nSearch\nSearch\nNew Patients Always Welcome!\nOpen 6 Days a Week in Hattiesburg\nAt The Pet Hospital (Parkway), we are open\nMonday through Saturday\n, offering a full range of veterinary services to ensure that your pets get the quality care they deserve.\nBook Online\n(601) 544-3290\nNew Patients Always Welcome!\nOpen 6 Days a Week in Hattiesburg\nAt The Pet Hospital (Parkway), we are open\nMonday - Saturday\noffering a full range of veterinary services to ensure that your pets get the quality care they deserve.\nBook Online\n(601) 544-3290\nNew Patients Always Welcome!\nOpen 6 Days a Week in Hattiesburg\nAt The Pet Hospital (Parkway), we are open\nMonday - Saturday\noffering a full range of veterinary services to ensure that your pets get the quality care they deserve.\nBook Online\n(601) 544-3290\nWe're Passionate About Pets!\nThe Pet Hospital (Parkway) Veterinarians in Hattiesburg Welcome Patients 6 Days a Week, Including Saturdays\nThe Pet Hospital (Parkway)offers comprehensive veterinary services for cats, dogs and exotic pets from Hattiesburg, Petal and surrounding areas.\nFrom\npreventive care\nand\nsurgery\nto\nacupuncture\n, our broad and varied service offering can meet all of your pet’s health needs in one place.\nWe care for companion animals in the Hattiesburg and Petal community and have earned a reputation for providing quality, professional care with a compassionate touch.\nWhether you are bringing your pet in for the first time or have relied on our veterinary team for years, we will treat them as if they were our own.\nAbout Our Hospital\nFear Free Certified Vets\nAll of our veterinarians at The Pet Hospital (Parkway) are Fear Free Certified Professionals who have received extensive training on how to create a calm, welcoming environment for pets.\nMeet Our Vets\nAbout Fear Free\nComplete Range of Services\nComprehensive Veterinary Care\nThe Pet Hospital (Parkway) offers comprehensive veterinary services for cats, dogs and exotic pets in Hattiesburg and Petal.\nAcupuncture\nLearn More\nSurgery\nLearn More\nDental Care\nLearn More\nVaccinations\nLearn More\nWellness Exams\nLearn More\nEmergency Care\nLearn More\nDr. Gibson is very honest and has helped tremendously with my Heeler's back issues that two other vets could not fix without surgery.\n- Janice P.\nHelpful Blogs\nTips & Advice From Our Team\nOur informative blogs at The Pet Hospital (Parkway) feature helpful tips and advice from our Hattiesburg vets that will help you keep your pets healthy and happy, whether you are looking for advice on parasite protection or information on common pet illnesses.\nVaccine Reactions in Dogs: Everything You Should Know\nWhile vaccinating your dog does come with a risk of reactions, the benefit of lifelong protection against serious illnesses and diseases far outweighs this risk. Here, our Hattiesburg vets discuss the potential side effects associated with common dog vaccinations.\nRead more\nHookworm in Dogs: Signs, Treatment & Prevention\nHookworms often cause gastrointestinal upset, inflammation in a dog's intestine, and a life-threatening reduction in red blood cells (anemia). In today's post, our Hattiesburg vets discuss hookworms in dogs and options for treatment and prevention.\nRead more\nWhat is the FVRCP cat vaccine?\nOur vets at  vets recommend the FVRCP vaccine for all cats. In this post, you'll learn how the FVRCP shot protects your cat's health.\nRead more\nSmall Animals. Big Hearts.\nOpen 6 Days a Week\nThe Pet Hospital (Parkway) proudly serves patients from Hattiesburg, Petal and surrounding areas\nMonday through Saturday\n.\nHours\nMonday:\n07:30 am - 05:30 pm\nTuesday:\n07:30 am - 05:30 pm\nWednesday:\n07:30 am - 05:30 pm\nThursday:\n07:30 am - 05:30 pm\nFriday:\n07:30 am - 05:30 pm\nSaturday:\n08:00 am - 12:00 pm\nSunday:\nClosed\nLocation\n2010 Evelyn Gandy Pkwy\nHattiesburg\nMS\n39401\nUS\nPhone Number\n(601) 544-3290\nContact Us\nNew Patients Welcome\nThe Pet Hospital (Parkway) is accepting new patients! Our experienced vets are passionate about the health of companion animals in Hattiesburg and Petal. Get in touch today to book your pet's first appointment.\nContact Us\nThe Pet Hospital (Parkway)\nHome\nAbout\nCore Care\nSurgery\nEmergencies\nPatients\nCareers\nContact\nPrivacy Policy\nDo Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\nTerms & Conditions\nAccessibility\nSearch\nSitemap\nBack to Top\nFacebook\nGoogleBusiness\nCopyright © 2026. All Rights Reserved.\nPart of the\nPetVet Care Centers Network\n.\nPanther\nContact Panther Location\nParkway\nContact Parkway Location\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\n×\nIMPORTANT NOTICE:\nDue to Hurricane Isaias, our hours and availability may be affected. Please call us before visiting to be we sure we are open and able to provide pet care at this time.\nCall\n(601) 544-3290\nOpen Modal",
